  "description": "A through-passage front to back with two rooms either side, repeated above. The passage receives the visitor without admitting them to a room, carries the stair, and draws air through the house. Symmetry is not applied to this plan; it is generated by it, which is why the diagram survives every change of ornament laid over it. WP-13.5 states the container the description always implied: the kitchen, pantry, breakfast room and powder room carry `block: service` and the back hall carries `hyphen: true`, so `geometry.blocks_for` lays the service programme into a dependency beyond a link and the main block carries the type's own rooms -- passage, stair hall, drawing room, dining room, library and the butler's pantry that joins the dining room to the link. Until then every room of this diagram was laid into one rectangle and the service programme sized the main block, which is what put eleven enclosed rooms inside a four-over-four.",
